    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 3f6d32169607015308a4472a2120f5146c753cdc -->\n**Needs changes before merge** - one pinning test fails against current main.\n\nThanks for the AltMill machines. Reviewed at head 3f6d321, trial-merged with main 440a6b8 (clean, no conflicts).\n\n**What looks good**\n- Three machine files, one `MACHINES` entry each; no new post, no dependency, no `build.rs` / `.github` / scripts change, no vendor post text or assets. Figures and their sources are in `docs/decisions/728-altmill.md`, and the 4x4 figures come from a real `$$`.\n- The files are internally consistent: travel and rates match the decision file, spindle 1200-24000 on all three, `safe_retract: 0.0` with the `G53 G0 Z0` lift before each `T<n> M6`, and no G43/G49.\n- The over-maximum spindle speed is refused by name (\"spindle rpm over machine maximum\").\n- No process files touched, so no `PROCESS_VERSION` bump is needed (main is 50). New test has a provenance header and a Gate map.\n\n**Local results (merged with main)**\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `altmill_machines` | 3 passed, 1 FAILED |\n| `machine` | 33 passed |\n| `machine_library` | 11 passed |\n| `grblhal_post` | 9 passed |\n| `conformance` | 6 passed |\n| clippy `camcraft-app` (`altmill_machines`, `machine`) `-D warnings` | clean |\n\n```\ntest the_4x4_two_tool_program_is_locked ... FAILED\ncrates/app/tests/altmill_machines.rs:142: crates/app/tests/golden/nc/grblhal/altmill_4x4_two_tool_inch.nc: run with WRITE_GOLDEN=1 and review the diff\n  left:  \"(Sienci AltMill 4x4)\\nG21 G17 G90 ...\"   (posted)\n  right: \"(Sienci AltMill 4x4)\\nG20 G17 G90 ...\"   (golden)\n```\n\n**Requested before merge**\n1. `crates/app/tests/altmill_machines.rs:129-142`: the inch case sets `inch[\"units\"] = json!(\"inch\")` on the mirrored machine. Since #902 (PR #981, now on main) the posted units come from the document, not the machine file, so the post still emits `G21` and the inch golden no longer matches. Drive inch the way `crates/app/tests/grblhal_post.rs` (`an_inch_document_posts_g20_and_inches`) does, by passing the document `Units: inch` post parameter, and drop the machine-side override. The golden `altmill_4x4_two_tool_inch.nc` then stays as it is. Please do not regenerate it blindly; confirm the diff is nil.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- The body says the branch is stacked on #715; that is already on main, so the diff is just the nine AltMill files.\n- The 2x4 and 4x8 figures remain spec-page only, as the PR says. Z travel is written `-L..L` (e.g. 4x4 `-170..170`) as the other shipped machines do, while the homed Z origin is the top; the decision file explains the choice.\n- Not exercised: the full workspace gate, the UI suites (no UI change), a machine run of my own.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
